config VIDEO_MTK_CAM_GRAPH
	bool
	select MEDIA_CONTROLLER
	select VIDEO_V4L2_SUBDEV_API
	select V4L2_ASYNC
	help
	  The media graph that ties the MediaTek MT6589 camera blocks together.

	  This driver owns no hardware.  It registers the struct media_device
	  and struct v4l2_device for the camera path, runs the
	  v4l2_async_notifier that pulls mtk-csi2-rx, mtk-scam and mtk-cam into
	  that v4l2_device, and creates the media links between them from the
	  "remote-endpoint" properties in the device tree.

	  Without it the three subdevs register as async subdevs that nothing is
	  waiting for, so no entity joins a media_device and no media_link is
	  ever created: the pads exist and the dtsi points them at each other,
	  but that is not a graph.

	  It is deliberately a silent bool selected by the three camera drivers
	  rather than a user-visible option: none of them can produce a graph
	  without it, so there is no configuration in which turning it off is
	  useful.  It also carries no depends of its own, because its three
	  selectors already depend on the SoC and adding a second, narrower
	  condition here would make Kconfig warn about selecting it with
	  unmet dependencies.